        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The report-density rule is framework review-process behavior, but it is being added inside every `.harness/custom/review-prompts/*` consumer-customizable severity policy. That crosses the harness-policy responsibility boundary: framework methodology should live in the framework-owned briefing/workflow surface, not under `.harness/custom`, where consumers can override or drift it independently.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": ".harness/custom/review-prompts/adr.md",
              "line": 13,
              "category": "responsibility-boundary cross"
            },
            {
              "message": "This adds a numeric-state rule to the new convention, but the paired reviewer-policy changes only add an `upstream restatement` finding class for prose restatement in impl-plan/types. Since the convention later claims enforcement through those severity-policy finding classes, the numeric rule is left as document-only guidance, contradicting the enforce-by-mechanism convention's requirement that new rules ship with an enforcement mechanism or reassess trigger.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md",
              "line": 30,
              "category": "convention contradiction"
            }
          ],
